ining consistent performance across long usage. Why semi-ceramic is the smarter upgrade Standard organic pads can feel softer and fade quicker under real riding conditions. Street Pro’s semi-ceramic compound is built for stronger bite, stable performance, and cleaner braking—so you get a noticeable upgrade without going extreme. Ideal For 🏙️ Daily city traffic 🛣️ Highway touring 🌧️ Rainy & wet conditions 🌀 Curves, flyovers & quick stops Upgrade your braking. Feel the difference. Switch to 66BHP Street Pro Semi-Ceramic Brake Pads for stronger stopping power, cleaner wheels, and confident control—every ride, every condition. *Braking performance may vary based on riding style, rotor condition, tyre grip, and installation quality.63:T461,Galfer HH Sintered Brake Pads are a type of brake pads used in high-performance motorcycles, ATVs, and other vehicles. They are made by the Spanish company Galfer, which specializes in braking systems for motorcycles and bicycles. Sintered brake pads are made by fusing metallic particles together under high pressure and heat. The resulting material is very dense and durable, with excellent resistance to heat and wear. This makes sintered brake pads ideal for high-performance applications where consistent braking performance is essential. Galfer HH Sintered Brake Pads are designed for aggressive riding and racing. They offer high levels of stopping power, even at high temperatures, and provide excellent feel and feedback to the rider. They are also resistant to fade and glazing, which can occur when brake pads get too hot and lose their friction properties. Fitment Note: Front Has 2 Calipers (Needs 2 Sets of Brake Pads) Front : FD138G1370 Rear : FD165G1371 Compatible Vehicle: Royal Enfield Himalayan (2020- Included Items: 1 Set Comes with 2 HH Sintered Brake Pads Which Fits One Caliper Instructions Manual64:T44f,Galfer HH Sintered Brake Pads are a type of brake pads used in high-performance motorcycles, ATVs, and other vehicles. They ar